adbd (1.0.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * usbdevice: add an optional CDC-NCM network function alongside adb in the
    same USB configuration. Enable it with ADBD_GADGET_NET=ncm; the default
    remains adb-only.
  * usbdevice: use the USB composite device class (0xEF/0x02/0x01) when NCM is
    enabled, so Windows enumerates the gadget as a composite device and uses
    its in-box NCM driver.
  * Add usbnetwork and usbnetwork.service: configure usb0, serve DHCP with
    dnsmasq and NAT the USB subnet to the board's default uplink. The service
    is a no-op unless ADBD_GADGET_NET=ncm.
  * Add the optional adbd-smb helper. Samba is recommended but not configured
    by default; `adbd-smb enable` adds the /home/robo share, sets the SMB
    password when needed, and starts smbd. `adbd-smb disable` reverses it.
  * Document the NCM network settings, the opt-in SMB share, and the
    Linux/Windows host setup.
  * Do not ship a Windows companion INF: Windows 10/11, Linux and macOS have
    in-box NCM drivers.

 -- wentywenty <2321901849@qq.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

adbd (1.0.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * usbdevice: load libcomposite/usb_f_fs before creating the gadget, so
    installation works before systemd-modules-load has run.
  * usbdevice: retry the configfs function link and UDC bind instead of
    waiting for FunctionFS "ready", which is not set before link on the
    RDK X5 6.1 kernel. This fixes the startup deadlock with adbd's
    FUNCTIONFS_BIND wait.
  * android-compat: derive brand/manufacturer from the device-tree compatible
    vendor, strip whitespace from platform fields, and support an optional
    /etc/android-compat.properties overlay.

 -- wentywenty <2321901849@qq.com>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 03:00:00 +0800

